  <section><h2>What it does</h2><p>Instead of a push notification, a scheduled reminder uses a phone call. The demo shows the app's user flow.</p></section>
  <section><h2>My contribution</h2><p>Shivam built the Kotlin and Jetpack Compose app and a pattern-based parser for entering tasks in natural language.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Parsing reminders</h2><p>The parser recognizes more than 80 input patterns, according to the project resume. Its exact coverage and evaluation method are not documented here.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Calls and platform constraints</h2><p>Phone calls are central to the reminder experience. Device permissions, operating-system behavior, and delivery reliability may vary; the linked demo shows the demonstrated flow.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Testing and limitations</h2><p>The project resume reports extensive testing, but the distinction between test cases and test suites needs confirmation. This page does not claim a verified test count or reduced manual-entry rate.</p></section>
